1
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:43,040
Hiccup Panic

2
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:50,620
We move a muscle called
the diaphragm up and down

3
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:53,380
and breathe by moving our lungs.

4
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:58,600
But when this diaphragm starts to spasm,

5
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:01,020
the rhythm of breathing gets thrown off,

6
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:03,040
the glottis at the back of the throat opens,

7
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:05,220
and air is suddenly expelled.

8
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:07,460
As a reaction, you inhale suddenly,

9
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:08,960
and that's the hiccup!

10
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:12,340
Got it?

11
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:18,980
Damn it, I have to rewrite it again?

12
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:20,480
Here.

13
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:25,080
Hold your breath and drink some water,
and your hiccups will stop, Ryo-chan.

14
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:28,040
I've already had water,
like ten glasses since this morning.

15
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:29,380
Is that so?

16
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:33,160
Someone must be talking about you, Ryo-san.

17
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,060
That's a sneeze, you know.

18
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:36,960
Right.

19
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:39,560
I wonder why hiccups
happen in the first place.

20
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:40,440
How would I know?

21
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:44,120
If I pass them to Terai,
maybe my hiccups will stop.

22
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:48,320
Hiccups aren't like yawns,
Ryo-san, they don't spread that way.

23
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:52,260
Just stay still and quiet,
and they'll stop before you know it.

24
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:53,560
Quiet?

25
00:02:55,820 --> 00:03:00,020
Then write this report in my place.

26
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:01,780
What kind of logic is that?

27
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:05,660
I'm taking a break until my hiccups stop.

28
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:08,100
You should write this yourself, Ryo-chan.

29
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:11,060
Anyway, I can't get any work
done until these hiccups stop.

30
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:12,080
I'm going to take a break.

31
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:12,740
Ugh.

32
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:15,560
I'm really counting on you.

33
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:17,580
Fine, I'll write it for you.

34
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:20,600
Because all you ever think
about is skipping work.

35
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:22,980
Back to you.

36
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:25,520
Kameyari is in the lead,
and next from our side is -

37
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:26,900
You're a cheeky little thing.

38
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:29,200
That was the afternoon news.

39
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:31,420
Damn it, every time I hiccup -

40
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:34,260
The screen keeps changing and I
can't make heads or tails of it.

41
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:37,720
I see. I don't need to be
holding the remote after all.

42
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:40,920
Honestly, I wish these
hiccups would hurry up and stop.

43
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,280
W-what is it, Reiko?

44
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:49,440
How about it? Did the hiccups stop?

45
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:52,120
So that's what you meant.

46
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:54,740
No good

47
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:56,380
Sorry about that.

48
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:01,660
It's me, Ryo-san.

49
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:03,340
What is it, Nakagawa?

50
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:05,160
How about it? Did the hiccups stop?

51
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,340
Good morning.

52
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:13,020
Did the hiccups stop, senpai?

53
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:15,940
That's enough, Nakagawa too!

54
00:04:17,140 --> 00:04:18,780
I was startled too.

55
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:20,960
Ryo-chan using his hiccups as an excuse

56
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:22,780
to skip work is just not right.

57
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:25,100
Don't make light of hiccups!

58
00:04:25,860 --> 00:04:28,780
If hiccups last too long,
it can be life-threatening,

59
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:30,740
you know.

60
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:32,720
You're overreacting.

61
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:34,560
That's right, senpai.

62
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:36,980
I remember hearing that as a kid.

63
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:39,300
That if your hiccups don't stop, you'll die.

64
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:41,040
No way, that's not true.

65
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:43,980
It's been three hours
since the hiccups started.

66
00:04:43,980 --> 00:04:47,280
More than I expected, it's wearing me out.

67
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:49,840
It's even hard to breathe.

68
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:51,460
Are you okay, Ryo-chan?

69
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:53,600
About ways to stop hiccups...

70
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,760
What other ones were there again?

71
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,360
The ones I know of are...

72
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:59,760
holding your breath and drinking water,

73
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:02,160
and having someone startle you.

74
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:03,860
I think there are others too,

75
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:06,240
which is exactly when

76
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:11,780
I'll go get Grandma
Hattori from Third Street.

77
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:15,880
Now that I'm here,
there's nothing to worry about.

78
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:17,400
What are you planning to do?

79
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,020
Water.

80
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:20,160
Here you go.

81
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:21,080
Okay.

82
00:05:21,670 --> 00:05:23,460
W-what are you -

83
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:25,060
Chopsticks.

84
00:05:25,570 --> 00:05:25,820
Here.

85
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:28,460
Go ahead.

86
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:31,580
Quick.

87
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:34,700
Alright, here we go.

88
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:35,240
Good work.

89
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:39,778
W-w-what...

90
00:05:39,828 --> 00:05:42,200
What are you doing!

91
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:44,440
Open your mouth.

92
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:45,100
Okay.

93
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:50,960
You drink one sip at a time from each
of the four sides of these chopsticks.

94
00:05:54,820 --> 00:05:57,080
N-no, stop, stop!

95
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:58,960
Okay,

96
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,480
See? It stopped, didn't it?

97
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:07,220
How about it, Ryo-chan?

98
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:08,500
Now that you mention it,

99
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:10,420
you're lucky, Ryo-san.

100
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:11,440
That's impressive, as expected.

101
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:15,220
This is the best cure for hiccups.

102
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:17,080
Well then, Ryo-san.

103
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:19,760
Whew, thank goodness, thank goodness.

104
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:21,720
Thanks a lot, old lady.

105
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:23,740
Don't mention it.

106
00:06:23,740 --> 00:06:25,660
Well, I'll be going now.

107
00:06:25,660 --> 00:06:26,240
Yeah.

108
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:29,380
Good for you, Ryo-san.

109
00:06:29,380 --> 00:06:30,240
Yeah.

110
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,780
Ryo-san.

111
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:39,680
That's ridiculous! All my grandkids
stopped hiccuping with this method.

112
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:42,360
No, no, not like that.

113
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,680
Old man Tamai.

114
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,580
Who's there?

115
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:47,220
Mr. Tamai from across the
street from the Hattori house.

116
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:49,640
Those two don't get along.

117
00:06:50,140 --> 00:06:51,200
What did you come here for?

118
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:53,420
To stop your hiccups, of course.

119
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:55,120
I was asked to do it.

120
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:58,140
You should be at home listening
to the radio or something.

121
00:06:58,140 --> 00:07:00,560
He's always like this, with that foul mouth.

122
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:03,380
Tch, he's so irritating, this old man.

123
00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:07,080
They always fight.
Both of you, please just go home.

124
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:12,280
Excuse me, what method did Mr.
Tamai use to stop his hiccups?

125
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:18,000
Lower your head a little more.

126
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:22,740
Are you okay, Ryo-san?

127
00:07:22,740 --> 00:07:24,180
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

128
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:25,960
No violence!

129
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,240
Please calm down.

130
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:29,340
What do you mean, "no violence"?

131
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:34,060
Either way, Ryo-chan,
your hiccups stopped, didn't they?

132
00:07:34,060 --> 00:07:39,240
Speaking of which, this time it's really

133
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:45,940
Hey, it hasn't stopped at all!
In the end, it's no good!

134
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:52,920
If it's Chuck, drinking water while tilting your head back works every time.
Who said that?

135
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,860
Tilt your chin up.

136
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:01,600
I hear there's a rugby
match on the nearby grounds.

137
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:05,040
But rugby's played on an oval field, right?

138
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:07,560
Yes, the others are out front.

139
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,500
Heave-ho, heave-ho!

140
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:10,420
Really.

141
00:08:11,020 --> 00:08:11,960
I drank it all!

142
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:19,240
I can't just drink water! Do I look
like some kind of stunt act to you?

143
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,880
That has nothing to do with it, you know.
Rugby...

144
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:25,100
Senpai, didn't it stop? The hiccups.

145
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:28,060
Stopped? Did it stop?

146
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:32,300
As long as the hiccups stop,
we're in the clear.

147
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:33,200
Thanks.

148
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:35,860
No good?

149
00:08:38,980 --> 00:08:41,260
Hey, Ryo-san, try drinking this.

150
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:44,240
I'm not drinking another drop of water.

151
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,880
It's not water, I'm telling you.

152
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:49,440
When hiccups wouldn't stop
back in my wife's hometown,

153
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:52,880
I remembered them brewing persimmon
stems and making someone drink it.

154
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:53,680
Persimmon stems.

155
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:55,900
Just try it, it's worth a shot.

156
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:58,460
What's this "worth a shot" nonsense?

157
00:08:59,060 --> 00:09:01,380
Anyway, just drink it.
Think of it as being tricked.

158
00:09:01,380 --> 00:09:03,700
Fine, but just a little.

159
00:09:04,140 --> 00:09:04,320
Yeah.

160
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:07,120
It's awful.

161
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:07,580
How is it?

162
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:14,980
Good for you.

163
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:19,800
Didn't work?

164
00:09:19,980 --> 00:09:22,610
Damn it, why? Why won't it stop?

165
00:09:22,660 --> 00:09:24,080
My hiccups

166
00:09:24,460 --> 00:09:26,680
won't stop even with persimmon stem tea

167
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:29,740
My kids' hiccups stopped with it, though.

168
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:32,000
Is Ryo-san here?

169
00:09:32,060 --> 00:09:33,660
He can't stop his hiccups?

170
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:37,020
After persimmon stems, it's tofu now?

171
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:40,560
For hiccups, this is the best remedy.

172
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:44,800
Well, sit down.

173
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:50,520
Do you know what tofu is made from, Ryo-san?

174
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:51,960
Tofu?

175
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:54,980
You have to answer what tofu is made from.

176
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:57,600
Soybeans, obviously.

177
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:01,260
What are you doing?

178
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:03,220
See, it stopped.

179
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,140
It stopped.

180
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:06,420
Really?

181
00:10:06,420 --> 00:10:08,000
It actually stopped?

182
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,320
All he did was answer "soybean."

183
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:11,020
Amazing.

184
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:13,040
That's groundbreaking.

185
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:15,440
No idea why, though.

186
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:19,620
Well, I've got the shop,
so I'm heading back.

187
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:20,560
Thanks.

188
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:23,220
No, no,
you've really done something impressive.

189
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:27,340
Hey, Ryo-san.

190
00:10:29,020 --> 00:10:30,240
I can't believe it.

191
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:33,960
No hiccups have ever refused
to stop with this before.

192
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:40,720
Ryo-san, he says his hiccups won't stop.

193
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:45,160
Does the greengrocer know
how to stop hiccups too?

194
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:47,134
Well, Ryo-san,

195
00:10:47,184 --> 00:10:49,680
eggplant works wonders for hiccups.

196
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:51,020
Eggplant?

197
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:53,920
That's right,
just think about an eggplant in your head.

198
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,380
Just think about it?

199
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:58,560
It's even more revolutionary.

200
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:00,780
Eggplant, he says, Ryo-chan.

201
00:11:00,780 --> 00:11:03,760
There are all kinds of eggplants, you know.

202
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:07,060
Like grilled eggplant or mapo eggplant.

203
00:11:07,460 --> 00:11:10,980
So you just picture a regular,
ordinary eggplant, right?

204
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:13,200
Yeah, just picture it floating in your head.

205
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:30,060
Even if you two imagine it,
my hiccups won't stop, you know.

206
00:11:30,880 --> 00:11:34,760
Ryo-san, focus your mind
and think only about eggplant.

207
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:40,580
Eggplant? Eggplant, eggplant, eggplant...
I don't get it.

208
00:11:40,580 --> 00:11:44,720
Now that I think about it,
only eggplant comes to mind -

209
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:51,220
but whenever I try to think of eggplant, green peppers,
tomatoes, onions, and lotus root keep popping up.

210
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:56,220
Ryo-san, calm down.

211
00:11:56,220 --> 00:11:57,340
It's that, that thing.

212
00:11:57,340 --> 00:12:00,160
You know,
the blue-purple one shaped like this.

213
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:01,780
I'll go buy an eggplant.

214
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:03,820
Rather than that,
drawing it would be faster.

215
00:12:03,820 --> 00:12:04,900
Eggplant, eggplant.

216
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:11,100
I'm pretty sure this is an eggplant,
Ryo-chan.

217
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:13,080
This is a Venus-nasu, you know.

218
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:16,100
A regular eggplant is more like this.

219
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:17,640
Like this.

220
00:12:18,340 --> 00:12:20,160
An eggplant is like this.

221
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:21,800
Wrong!

222
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:22,500
Like this!

223
00:12:22,940 --> 00:12:24,840
An eggplant is like this!

224
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:29,420
It's fine, I said!

225
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:30,540
If it's eggplant, anything goes!

226
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:33,100
Eggplant, eggplant, eggplant, eggplant!

227
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:35,040
Eggplant, eggplant!

228
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:37,680
Ryo-chan, you remembered the eggplant!

229
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:41,640
Good for you, Ryo-san.

230
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:42,100
Yeah.

231
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:43,700
Thanks, everyone.

232
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:46,180
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

233
00:12:46,180 --> 00:12:48,640
Banzai! Banzai! Ban...

234
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:15,240
I've heard that too.

235
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:18,380
When we were kids,
they said if hiccups don't stop, you'll die.

236
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:21,900
No way anyone actually died from hiccups!

237
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:22,620
Kankichi.

238
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:24,840
Kankichi.

239
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:27,520
You pocketed the shop's sales, didn't you?

240
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:29,060
Mom.

241
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:32,220
She's saying you stole money from our house,
you know.

242
00:13:32,220 --> 00:13:33,400
So, what's the story?

243
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:35,100
What's this all of a sudden?

244
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:36,680
Maybe when I was a kid, but...

245
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:41,920
Well, I've borrowed a bit of snack food for my sake now and then,
I admit.

246
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:45,000
But I've never laid a finger on the money,
not ever.

247
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:46,860
Snacks for sake, you say?

248
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:49,500
So the goods from Ise have
been disappearing bit by bit?

249
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,040
So that was your doing!

250
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:54,080
Well, that's...

251
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:56,220
Good heavens, sit down right here.

252
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:58,640
Our merchandise! What a disaster!

253
00:13:58,640 --> 00:14:00,860
Mom, this is a workplace!

254
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:04,000
I have my own say in this, you know.

255
00:14:04,900 --> 00:14:06,800
Things are getting really out of hand here.

256
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:11,040
I wonder if Ryo-san got scolded like
that all the time when he was a kid too.

257
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:12,220
Oh dear, what a predicament.

258
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:13,460
How embarrassing.

259
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:15,380
Mom, thank you so much.

260
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:20,060
Oh my, I can't believe I
lost my composure like that.

261
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:21,160
